.TH SAPHIRA-INSTALL 8 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
saphira-install \- install a Saphira profile into a mounted target
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-install
.B --target
.I TARGET
.B --profile
.I PROFILE
.RB [ --reinstall ]
.RB [ --repository
.IR REPO ]
.RB [ --hostname
.IR NAME ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saphira-install
is the disk-targeting frontend to
.BR saphira-assemble-rootfs (8):
it installs a profile into the mounted filesystem at
.IR TARGET .
The assembled system is identical whether it lands on a disk image,
a disk partition, or a plain directory \-
one assembler, no separate installer package list, so a profile that
builds a working image always installs a working system.
.PP
After assembly,
.BR saphira-genfstab (8)
entries for the target's live mounts are appended to
.I TARGET/etc/fstab
(skipped lines already present; plain directories yield no entries
and are harmlessly skipped).
.PP
.B --reinstall
wipes the target's contents first and reinstalls from scratch.
Preservation options (keep users, keep data, keep config) are future
work; for now reinstall keeps nothing.
.PP
Requires root privileges. Whole-disk partitioning, filesystem
creation and bootloader installation belong to
.BR saphira-image (8);
this tool starts where the filesystem is already mounted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --target " " \fITARGET
Mounted target directory (required).
.TP
.BR --profile " " \fIPROFILE
Profile name from
.BR saphira-profiles (5)
(required).
.TP
.B --reinstall
Wipe a non-empty target and reinstall instead of refusing.
.TP
.BR --repository " " \fIREPO
APK repository, passed through to the assembler (default: host
configuration).
.TP
.BR --hostname " " \fINAME
Hostname to write (default: the profile name).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_PROFILE_ROOT
Profile directory (default
.IR /usr/share/saphira/profiles ).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_REPOSITORY
Same effect as
.BR --repository .
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_HOSTNAME
Same effect as
.BR --hostname .
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_ROOT_PASSWORD
Passed through to the assembler (boot-test images only).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_ASSEMBLER
Assembler binary (default: alongside this tool).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_GENFSTAB
.B saphira-genfstab
binary (default: alongside this tool).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Installed (and fstab updated where applicable).
.TP
.B 1
Any failure; the target is left in place for diagnosis.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install the virtualisation host onto a mounted disk:
.PP
.RS
sudo saphira-install --target /mnt/saphira \\
    --profile virtualisation-host \\
    --repository /out/stage4/packages/hatched
.RE
.PP
Rebuild the same disk from installer media, keeping nothing:
.PP
.RS
sudo saphira-install --target /mnt/saphira \\
    --profile virtualisation-host --reinstall
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira-assemble-rootfs (8),
.BR saphira-profiles (5),
.BR saphira-bootstrap (8),
.BR saphira-genfstab (8)
